# r1113 Power Grid rerun pwg17r on jar jar_archive/pwg_gate/backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-17.jar (sha1 cbc2ddee37ca,
# the same jar as pwg17). Reruns only the pwg17 rows that were BATCH-FAULT or INCONCLUSIVE and still need numbers
# (verdicts: perf/runs/r1113/verdicts/pwg17.md), plus the setup rows they depend on. Fixes in this batch and the probes:
#   SQ-PWG-90  boot regex "phase 10(.0)?" (the jar logs "phase 10.0)"); zpwg10 check no longer calls Ingredient.getItems
#              (hidden in Rhino: getStacks) nor Recipe.getType (the recipe lines print serializer= now); the ponder
#              structure part (zpwg5 nbtall) passed in pwg17 and is left out, so no ponder datapack is needed
#   SQ-PWG-91  wrench "got:" no longer lists the wrench itself; the drops lines stay: they FAIL on -17 (port bug, the
#              four ceiling_tile_* loot tables roll one of two entries), two extra drops reads show the random pick
#   SQ-PWG-95  zpwg10 cord: Pattern through getOrCreateTag (setTag is not visible), no getUUID in the cord line
#   SQ-PWG-94  same circuit at new Z plus zpwg10 node (voltage, saved value, index, network of each terminal), zpwgg net,
#              and a control with a plain powergrid:wire_connector in the same place (Z 2054)
#   SQ-PWG-73  zpwg9b cord: no Vec3 .x/.y/.z passed into Java (FieldAndMethods NPE escaped the catch after "cord step
#              4"), no ItemStack.getTag; menus closed with doCloseContainer only (closeContainer is not visible)
#   SQ-PWG-80, -81, -82  mixer and arm driven by a cogwheel (axis y) east of them with a creative motor on it facing
#              down: both are cog-only (MechanicalMixerBlock.hasShaftTowards is false), the pwg17 gearbox ran at 64 and
#              they stayed at 0. Shows read the cog (X+1) and the motor (X+1, Y+1) instead of gearbox and motor
#   SQ-PWG-76, -78, -79 run again only as the chain's setup (chain board, schematic, unetched circuit for -80)
# Not repeated (PASS from the pwg17 numbers): SQ-PWG-92, -93, -96, -84, -72, -83, -85, -88, -89, -63.
# FRESH WORLD (level pwg17r): the pwg17 world holds the first run's tables, wires, cords, gearboxes and a basin with the
# unetched circuit in it, so the same coordinates would not start clean.
# Group A superflat, level pwg17r, spawn-animals=true, ground Y -61 (grass), blocks at Y -60. Each area's SETUP row kills
# the animals generated in its chunks. The world is peaceful.
# Areas (no block overlap):
#   P10    X 1095 to 1135, Z 1995 to 2085 (SQ-PWG-90 forceload; -91 Z 2010 to 2011, -94 Z 2050 to 2054, -95 Z 2060)
#   P9b    X 1090 to 1130, Z 1805 to 1850 (SQ-PWG-SETUP14A forceload; -73 Z 1810 to 1825)
#   P9c    X 1135 to 1200, Z 1855 to 1915 (SQ-PWG-76 forceload; mixer cogs X+1 of each mixer at Y -58, motors on them at
#          Y -57; arm cogs X+1 of each arm at Y -60, motors on them at Y -59)
# Prep (INST = the instance root; all before the boot):
#   COPYDEV=1 PGJAR=$INST/jar_archive/pwg_gate/backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-17.jar prep_srv.sh OUT pwg17r A spawn-animals=true
#     (PGJAR is required: prep_srv.sh drops every Power Grid jar unless it is given)
#   ls OUT/srv/mods | grep -i -E 'powergrid|cc-tweaked'   (only backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-17.jar); sha1sum of the
#     jar starts cbc2ddee37ca
#   for p in $INST/tools/scratch_query/pwg_*.js; do cp "$p" OUT/srv/kubejs/server_scripts/zz_$(basename "$p"); done
#     (thirteen probes, the CURRENT copies)
#   ls OUT/srv/kubejs/server_scripts/zz_pwg_*.js | wc -l      (13)
#   grep -c 'cogdrive' OUT/srv/kubejs/server_scripts/zz_pwg_p9c_probe.js         (non-zero: the pwg17r p9c)
#   grep -c "cmd == 'node'" OUT/srv/kubejs/server_scripts/zz_pwg_p10_probe.js    (1: the pwg17r p10)
#   grep -c 'doCloseContainer' OUT/srv/kubejs/server_scripts/zz_pwg_p9b_probe.js (non-zero: the pwg17r p9b)
#   Loading Protection (as pwg10 to pwg17):
#   python3 $INST/tools/scratch_query/qrun.py toml OUT/srv/config/loadingprotection-common.toml '"Loading Protection Configuration"' protectionDuration 1
#   Nothing else: no ponder datapack, no CC program, no config edit.
# Run: qrun.py run OUT tools/scratch_query/batches/r1113/pwg17r.qb perf/runs/r1113/pwg17r
# Probe goggle reads log a RuntimeDistCleaner ERROR (client class): no blanket ERROR reject.
# waitlog matches anywhere since the row start; real waits are sleeps (20 ticks = 1 s) plus pace (s after each command).
pace 1

